## Run History

### Runs 1–6 — Baseline CCE, Narrow Backbone

```
Loss:     Categorical Cross-Entropy (equal weights)
Backbone: stem=8, max_filters=64
Size:     28.8 KB
```

**Problem:** Class imbalance collapse. CCE applied equal loss to all 144 grid cells. The model learned to always predict `recyclable` or `biodegradable` — maximising total accuracy by ignoring rare classes.

| Class | Recall |
|---|---|
| General | ~0.30 ❌ |
| Recyclable | ~0.60 ❌ |
| Biodegradable | ~0.90 ✅ |
| Metal | ~0.15 ❌ |

---

### Runs 7–10 — Background Weight Suppression

```
Change:   BG_WEIGHT = 0.05 (down-weight background cells in loss)
Size:     28.8 KB
```

**Problem:** Dead end. The whole-image labelling scheme means every one of the 144 cells per image carries the object class — there are **no true background cells** to suppress. The tweak had zero mathematical effect.

| Class | Recall |
|---|---|
| General | ~0.40 ❌ |
| Recyclable | ~0.55 ❌ |
| Biodegradable | ~0.88 ✅ |
| Metal | ~0.25 ❌ |

---

### Runs 11–13 — Manual Class Weight Boosting

```
Change:   CLASS_WEIGHTS = [1.0, 3.0, 1.0, 1.0, 4.0]  (general 3×, metal 4×)
          Adaptive callback adjusting weights every 5 epochs
Size:     28.8 KB
```

**Problem:** Class weight seesaw. Every boost to `metal` recall caused `recyclable` to collapse, and vice versa. The model's single 128-dim GAP vector cannot simultaneously represent both confused pairs at 96×96. Adaptive callbacks caused wild oscillation — `recyclable` jumped `90% → 14% → 62%` across consecutive epochs.

| Class | Recall (Run 13) |
|---|---|
| General | ~0.50 ❌ |
| Recyclable | ~0.35 ❌ |
| Biodegradable | ~0.85 ✅ |
| Metal | ~0.70 |

---

### Run 14 — Focal Loss `γ=2` 🔥 Breakthrough

```
Change:   Loss = CCE  →  Focal Loss (γ=2)
          FL = −(1 − p_t)² × log(p_t)
Size:     28.8 KB
```

**Why it worked:** The modulating factor `(1 − p_t)²` down-weights easy correct predictions (the sea of biodeg cells whose loss was swamping the gradient) and forces the model to focus on hard/misclassified samples (`general`, `metal`). **First run where all 4 classes exceeded 0.60 recall simultaneously.**

| Class | Recall | vs. Runs 1–6 |
|---|---|---|
| General | 0.61 | +0.31 ⬆️ |
| Recyclable | 0.63 | +0.03 ⬆️ |
| Biodegradable | 0.70 | −0.20 (acceptable trade-off) |
| Metal | 0.78 | +0.63 ⬆️⬆️ |

